{
  "id": "elicitation",
  "term": "elicitation",
  "definition": "In psychology, elicitation is the process of bringing out a targeted response, such as an emotion, by presenting a stimulus designed to evoke it. In research on emotion, this often means using culturally relevant materials to produce and study specific feelings and their intensity or pleasantness.",
